<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://erlangen-crm.org/current/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://erlangen-crm.org/current/E33_Linguistic_Object> .
<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> "isDirectTranslationOf"@en .
<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "To indicate where the Scribe worked from a lost translation/version or series of translations/versions to produce the target LinguisticObject. This relation should be used when we know that one LinguisticObject is a source of another (in a different language) and we want to assert that one text is not a direct translation from a previous document but where other unknown documents were involved in the process of going from one to another.\n\nFor comparing between text of the same language, or comparing between different languages where the direction of translation is unknown or indirect"@en .
<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is indirect translation of"@en .
<http://purl.org/saws/ontology#isIndirectTranslationOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
